&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Our vision is to give everyone the belief they can make their move. We aim to make moving simpler, by giving everyone the best place to turn to and return to for access to the tools, expertise, trust, and belief to make it happen.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re home to the UK’s largest choice of properties and are the go-to destination for millions of people planning their next move, reading the latest industry news, or just browsing what’s on the market.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data Quality Executive&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Location: Milton Keynes (Hybrid working, 2 days per week in the office. Tues/Weds)&lt;br&gt;Team: Customer Experience - Data Quality&lt;br&gt;Reports to: Data Quality Team Leader&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;An exciting opportunity has emerged to join the Data Quality Team as a Data Quality Executive at the UK’s number one property portal. Our partners are at the heart of everything we do, which means that we want to make things easy and right for them first time, every time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a member of Rightmove’s Data Quality Team you’ll play an important part in ensuring what’s displayed on Rightmove is accurate, fair and never misleading. Specifically, your role will focus on being the first point of contact for partners and consumers, content moderation, triaging inbound queries, and referring cases for assessment by the Data Quality Advisors when appropriate.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This role will include:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor, moderate, and upload advert content to ensure alignment with legislation and Rightmove’s Technical and Text Content Guidelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Approve and verify reviews, ensuring authenticity and adherence to the DMCCA legislation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track review similarity and duplication, identifying patterns and potential misuse.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Triage and manage incoming queries, meeting SLAs and performance targets while escalating high-priority cases to Data Quality Advisors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain proactive communication with the Data Quality Team Leader and Manager, flagging risks and requesting support when needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage with consumers, and partners to request review amendments, additional evidence, or identification where necessary, ensuring all communication is clear, compliant and relevant.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as first point of contact for sensitive or complex queries, resolving concerns with professionalism and empathy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support continuous improvement, identifying process enhancements within the Data Quality team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Promote adoption of self-service tools and initiatives, encouraging partner engagement and providing clear guidance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We’re looking for someone who:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Takes responsibility for their own workload, and for that of the team. You should be able to work under your own initiative and be self-motivating, determined to ensure the Data Quality inbox is always within our team targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Is a great communicator. You’ll be happy to speak up when you’ve seen an area for improvement, or to raise a priority case to the Data Quality Team Leader or Manager.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Is proactive and shares honestly and early. If you notice that inbound enquiries are increasing, you’ll bring it to the attention of the Data Quality Team Leader and arrange support to ensure we stay within our team targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Has great knowledge of our Technical Guidelines, Text Content Guidelines, Terms and Conditions and relevant regulatory legislation showing sound judgement when assessing inbound queries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Is able to demonstrate understanding and empathy towards the people you speak to. Data Quality is an emotive subject, and it’s important we handle all queries sensitively, whilst working towards a prompt resolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Has great prioritisation skills, is able to appreciate urgency and act accordingly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Has excellent relationship building skills, able to form relationships with partners and Rightmovers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Has good understanding of GDPR and ensures all forms of communication are compliant.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Has exceptional written and verbal communication skills with high attention to detail.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Is proficient in Microsoft office, particularly Outlook, Excel and Word.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 4, 67);&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Rightmove&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our vision is to give everyone the belief that they can make their move. We aim to make moving simpler by giving everyone the best place to turn to and return to for access to the tools, expertise, trust and belief to make it happen.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re home to the UK&#39;s largest choice of properties, and are the go-to destination for millions of people planning their next move, reading the latest industry news, or just browsing what&#39;s on the market.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Despite this growth, we’ve remained a friendly, supportive place to work, with employee #1 still working here!&amp;nbsp; We’ve done this by placing the Rightmove Hows at the heart of everything we do. These are the essential values that reflect our culture, and include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We&amp;nbsp;create&amp;nbsp;value…&lt;/strong&gt;by delivering results and building trust with partners and consumers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We&amp;nbsp;think&amp;nbsp;bigger…&lt;/strong&gt;by acting with curiosity and setting bold aspirations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We&amp;nbsp;care&amp;nbsp;deeply…&lt;/strong&gt;by being real, having fun, and valuing diversity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We&amp;nbsp;move&amp;nbsp;together…&lt;/strong&gt;by being one team - internally collaborative, externally competitive.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We&amp;nbsp;make&amp;nbsp;a difference…&lt;/strong&gt;by focusing on delivering measurable impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe in careers that open doors and help our team develop by providing an open and inclusive work environment, offering ongoing training opportunities, and supporting charity fundraising events. And with &lt;strong&gt;88% of Rightmovers saying we’re a great place to work&lt;/strong&gt;, we’re clearly doing something right!&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 4, 67);&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;img style=&quot;max-width: 100%;&quot;&gt;What we offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cash plan for dental, optical and physio treatments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Private Medical Insurance, Pension and Life Insurance, Employee Assistance Plan.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;27 days holiday plus two (paid) volunteering days a year to give back, and holiday buy schemes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contributory stakeholder pension.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Life assurance at 4x your basic salary to a spouse, family member or other nominated person in your life.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive compensation package.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Paid leave for maternity, paternity, adoption &amp;amp; fertility.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travel Loans, Bike to Work scheme, Rental Deposit Loan.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Charitable contributions through Payroll Giving and donation matching.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Access deals and discounts on things like travel, electronics, fashion, gym memberships, cinema discounts and more.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We offer hybrid working with a minimum of 2 days in the office. For our roles, such as Field or Home-based positions, different working arrangements apply - full details will be shared during the recruitment process.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 222, 180);&quot;&gt;&lt;img style=&quot;max-width: 100%;&quot; src=&quot;https://www.rightmove.co.uk/careers/content/uploads/2026/09/Untitled-30-July-2026-at-10.03.05-6.png&quot; alt=&quot;If all of this has caught your eye, you may well be a Rightmover in the making - Banner image&quot; width=&quot;1000&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;em&gt;As an Equal Opportunity Employer, Rightmove will never discriminate based on age, disability, sex, race, religion or belief, gender reassignment, marriage / civil partnership, pregnancy/maternity or sexual orientation.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;At Rightmove, we believe that a diverse and inclusive workforce leads to better innovation, productivity, and overall success., We are committed to creating a welcoming and inclusive environment for all employees, regardless of their background or identity, to develop and promote a diverse culture that reflects the communities we serve.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;By applying, you confirm that you are aged at least 18 or over and&amp;nbsp;that you’ve read and understood our &lt;a class=&quot;decorated-link&quot; href=&quot;https://www.rightmove.co.uk/c/privacy-policy/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-start=&quot;192&quot; data-end=&quot;259&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-start=&quot;193&quot; data-end=&quot;211&quot;&gt;Privacy Policy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, which explains how we handle and protect your personal information during the recruitment process.&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;*This position is fully remote/home based. Applications will be accepted from candidates based in the UK and the following US states: FL, IL, MA, MD, NY, PA, TX, VA.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Summary&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Associate Director, Publishing provides strategic leadership for the PLOS journal portfolio, ensuring that portfolio priorities, publishing investments, and journal development strategies align with organizational goals and advance PLOS&#39;s mission.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting to the Director, Publishing &amp;amp; Publishing Operations, the Associate Director leads and develops a team of Publishers responsible for the performance and strategic development of journals portfolios. The Associate Director serves as the primary steward of portfolio-wide publishing performance, translating organizational strategy into clear priorities and ensuring effective coordination across the organization.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Associate Director uses publishing data, financial information, market intelligence, and research community insight to guide strategic decisions, establish priorities, identify opportunities for growth and innovation, and manage risks. Working in partnership with the Director, Publishing &amp;amp; Publishing Operations, the Associate Director ensures that journal-level strategies collectively support a sustainable PLOS portfolio with a strong value proposition.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Supervisory Responsibilities&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead, develop, and support a team of senior publishing professionals responsible for journal and subject portfolio performance.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish clear goals, priorities, and measures of accountability that align with organizational and portfolio strategy.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide coaching, professional development, succession planning, and performance management for direct reports.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foster a culture of collaboration, inclusion, accountability, innovation, and continuous improvement.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Publishers to ensure effective leadership and development of Journal Development Managers and other publishing staff.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Portfolio Strategy and Performance&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and implement a portfolio-wide publishing strategy aligned with PLOS&#39;s mission and organizational objectives.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure that journal and subject portfolio strategies collectively support a clear and differentiated value proposition for the PLOS portfolio.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead regular portfolio reviews and develop recommendations regarding journal positioning, growth opportunities, performance, and future direction.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Balance the needs of individual journals and research communities with broader portfolio and organizational objectives.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support Publishers in identifying and responding to changes in research communities, funding policies, scholarly communication, and the publishing market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop consistent approaches and decision-making frameworks for evaluating proposals, opportunities, and performance across the portfolio.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Guide the evaluation and development of new journals, products, services, publishing models in line with PLOS’s strategic direction.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic and Business Leadership&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate organizational strategy into clear portfolio priorities, objectives, and plans for the publishing team.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee publishing budgets and forecasts in partnership with the Director and Publishers, ensuring responsible decision-making and effective resource allocation.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a thought partner to, and deputize for, the Director, Publishing &amp;amp; Publishing Operations when appropriate.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In close collaboration with colleagues in Editorial, Sales and Global Publishing Development, support publishers in developing impactful relationships with Editors-in-Chief, Editorial Board members, researchers, institutions, societies, and partner organizations.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build productive partnerships across Editorial, Publishing Operations, Sales &amp;amp; Global Publishing Development, Product, Technology, Marketing, Finance, Research Integrity, and other organizational teams.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Editorial and Publishing Operations leaders to ensure that journal strategies are supported by effective policies, processes, services, and quality standards.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Marketing and Communications to strengthen journal positioning, audience engagement, portfolio visibility, and demand generation.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Leadership and Culture&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Model the culture and behaviors PLOS is seeking to build, actively driving the culture change the organization needs through this transformation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a collaborative leader across PLOS, fostering strong cross-functional partnerships and organizational alignment that enable shared organizational priorities to be delivered successfully.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead change effectively by ensuring a clear strategic rationale, defined outcomes, appropriate measures of success, realistic resource requirements and clear accountability and decision-making.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications &amp;amp; Skills&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree or equivalent experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Business problem solver – operates with curiosity to get to the root of the business problem to ensure the ultimate solution is grounded in PLOS’s strategy and mission.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Substantial experience launching Open Access journals from proposal to publication.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong commercial and financial skills, including experience with budgeting, forecasting, business planning and P&amp;amp;L ownership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Substantial experience in STM publishing with progressively increased responsibility.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing senior publishing professionals, or comparable portfolio leaders.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to develop and execute strategic plans that deliver measurable business and operational outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong track record of leading and developing high-performing, geographically distributed teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional communication, relationship-building, and stakeholder management skills across cultures, disciplines, and organizational functions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Dedication to open access and transforming scholarly communication, with a genuine interest in engaging productively with the scientific community.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading high-volume journal portfolios and/or megajournals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Physical Requirements and Work Environment&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prolonged periods stationary at a desk and working on a computer.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Some national and international travel may be required.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Some flexibility to work across time zones may be required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The base salary range we’ve established for these positions is (&lt;strong&gt;US): $145,000- $157,000 or (UK) £90,000- £104,000&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;PLOS also offers a comprehensive benefits package summarized below.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;BENEFITS:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;US:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401k with employer match&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employee sponsored health, dental and vision insurance (Dental and Vision 100% employer paid)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Paid Vacation, 11 public holidays and sick leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Parental leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Birthday and three winter holidays days off&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Short term and long term disability insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2 days paid time off for volunteering per year&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fully remote work environment with stipend on joining for home office&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;UK:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Private medical insurance&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Life assurance&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Income protection &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Personal accident insurance&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Pension with up to 10% employer match&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;25 days holidays, market competitive Maternity and Paternity leave&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Birthday and three winter holidays days off&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;2 days paid time off for volunteering per year&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;Fully remote work environment with stipend on joining for home office&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About PLOS&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Building on a strong legacy of pioneering innovation, PLOS continues to be a catalyst in open science, reimagining models to meet open science principles, removing barriers and promoting inclusion in knowledge creation and sharing, and publishing research outputs that enable everyone to learn from, reuse and build upon scientific knowledge.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our work is supported by a highly skilled global in-house team, partnerships with local scholarly organizations, and the valued contributions of a diverse, international community of scientific researchers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We’re committed to equal opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re working to create a more equitable system of scientific knowledge and understanding. Removing barriers to inclusion and facilitating broad participation of voices is core to our success, inside and out.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Beyond accepting distinct perspectives, we seek and support divergent backgrounds among our staff because we know differences strengthen our teams, our work, and our communities. We strongly encourage applicants of all identities to join us as we work towards a future where science is open to all, for all.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Visit&lt;a href=&quot;http://plos.org/careers&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;plos.org/careers&lt;/a&gt; to learn more.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;To learn more about how PLOS protects your privacy, see our &lt;a href=&quot;https://plos.org/employee-privacy-notice/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Employee Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Summary:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking an experienced Senior Research Associate / Associate Scientist to join our Molecular Biology platform within the High Throughput Laboratory.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting to the Scientific Manager, this role will be responsible for delivering high-quality molecular biology workflows that underpin Quotient&#39;s somatic genomics platform. Working closely with Histology, Flow Cytometry, Assay Development, Automation and Data Science, you will support the processing of human tissue-derived samples from nucleic acid extraction through to sequencing-ready libraries.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The successful candidate will combine excellent technical expertise with a passion for continuous improvement, working collaboratively across scientific teams to optimise workflows, troubleshoot technical challenges and help implement new technologies into routine laboratory operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is ideally suited to someone who enjoys operating in a fast-paced biotechnology environment, is passionate about molecular biology, and is excited by the opportunity to contribute to a growing high-throughput genomics platform.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute high-quality molecular biology workflows including DNA and RNA extraction from human tissues and isolated cells/nuclei.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform nucleic acid quantification, quality assessment and fragmentation to support downstream sequencing applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare high-quality NGS libraries using a variety of library preparation methodologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support implementation, optimisation and routine operation of automated molecular biology workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshoot molecular biology workflows, identifying opportunities to improve quality, reproducibility and throughput.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with Histology and Flow Cytometry teams to ensure seamless progression of samples through the High Throughput Laboratory.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support implementation of new technologies and molecular biology methods developed by Assay Development into routine laboratory operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain accurate laboratory records using Benchling and associated laboratory information systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure compliance with laboratory quality systems, the Human Tissue Act, COSHH and all relevant laboratory procedures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to SOP development, protocol optimisation and continuous improvement initiatives across the Molecular Biology platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support training and mentoring of junior Research Associates where appropriate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;u&gt;Essential&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;BSc, MSc or equivalent experience in Molecular Biology, Genetics, Biochemistry or a related life science discipline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Significant hands-on experience working within a molecular biology laboratory (typically 3–5+ years in industry or equivalent).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience extracting high-quality DNA and RNA from a variety of biological sample types.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience performing nucleic acid fragmentation and quality assessment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience preparing Next Generation Sequencing (NGS) libraries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience operating within a high-throughput laboratory environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using laboratory automation or supporting automated molecular biology workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent laboratory organisation, troubleshooting and problem-solving skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working under the Human Tissue Act and associated quality systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using ELN/LIMS platforms (Benchling preferred).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication skills and the ability to work effectively within multidisciplinary scientific teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;u&gt;Desirable&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with NanoSeq or similar ultra-sensitive sequencing assays.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of somatic genomics, mutation detection and cancer genomics workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with Fixed and fresh frozen tissue.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience preparing sequencing libraries for low-input or challenging biological samples.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting implementation of automated liquid handling systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working collaboratively with Assay Development and Automation teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience within a rapidly growing biotechnology organisation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of laboratory process optimisation and Operational Excellence methodologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Values and Behaviors:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Encourage respectful disagreement and cultivate open-minded, ego-free interactions to continuously push each other towards excellence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Seek out diverse perspectives; practice active listening and genuine curiosity to ensure all contributions are valued, regardless of source&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recognize the impact of your behavior, language and attitudes, and strive for balanced, meaningful exchanges that enhance mutual growth and understanding in all interactions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use a company-first mindset to guide decision-making; prioritize team over individual success&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take calculated risks and challenge convention in the quest for exceptional outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Quotient:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Quotient Therapeutics is a privately-held, early stage company developing breakthrough medicines informed by natural somatic genetic diversity present in patients. Through our work in somatic genomics, we are forging a new status quo for biopharma research and development across a broad pipeline of internal and partnered programs.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The company was founded by Flagship Pioneering, an innovative enterprise that conceives, creates, resources, and grows first-in-category life sciences companies. Flagship Pioneering has created over 100 groundbreaking companies over the past twenty years, all of which are pioneering novel and proprietary biological, industrial, and engineering approaches to solve major needs in human health and sustainability. These companies include Moderna (MRNA), Generate Biomedicines, Sana Biotechnology (SANA), Tessera Therapeutics, Evelo Biosciences (EVLO), Indigo Agriculture, Seres Therapeutics (MCRB), and Syros Pharmaceuticals (SYRS).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Quotient Therapeutics and Flagship Pioneering are committed to equal employment opportunity regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity or Veteran status.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Recruitment &amp;amp; Staffing Agencies:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Quotient Therapeutics (“Quotient”) and Flagship Pioneering (“FSP”) do not accept unsolicited resumes from any source other than candidates. The submission of unsolicited resumes by recruitment or staffing agencies to Quotient, FSP or their employees is strictly prohibited unless contacted directly by Flagship Pioneering’s internal Talent Acquisition team. Any resume submitted by an agency in the absence of a signed agreement will automatically become the property of FSP, and FSP will not owe any referral or other fees with respect thereto.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Privacy Notice for Applicants:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;When you apply for a role at Flagship Pioneering or one of its portfolio companies, we collect and use personal information you provide (such as your name, contact details, work history, and application materials) to evaluate your application, communicate with you, and comply with legal obligations. Your application data is processed through Greenhouse, our applicant tracking system, and may also be reviewed using AI-assisted screening tools. We do not sell your personal information. California residents have rights under the CCPA/CPRA including to know, delete, and opt out of the sharing of their personal information. If you are located in the EU or UK, we process your data under GDPR and you have rights to access, rectify, and erase your data. To exercise your rights or for questions, contact -----<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Us:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Betty is an innovative entertainment company pioneering at the intersection of real-money online casinos and casual mobile gaming.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Betty Canada&amp;nbsp;is a scale up company accredited by the Alcohol and Gaming Commission of Ontario (AGCO) as a B2C operator in February 2023, we&#39;ve set a new standard in the industry.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Our mission is to redefine the online casino experience by offering a uniquely transparent environment where players can relax, unwind, and enjoy themselves safely. We are committed to accessibility, fairness, and inclusivity, fostering a community of like-minded individuals who value ethical gaming practices and prioritize our players&#39; safety and enjoyment above everything else.&lt;/p&gt;
